          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Historically, a motivation for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Tait"} Peter Tait
            to start thinking about classification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knots"} knots
            was the book
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lord+Kelvin"}> Lord Kelvin
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+Vortex+Atoms"} On Vortex Atoms
          %p
            which presented the speculation in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            that
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atoms"} atoms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+particles"} elementary particles
            are fundamentally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vortices"} vortices
            in a
            = succeed "-filling" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          %p Expositions of modern knot theory:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                J. Hoste, M. Thistlethwaite, J. Weeks:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The First 1,701,936 Knots
                %strong 20
                (1998) 33–48 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF03025227"}> doi:10.1007/BF03025227
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Sam Nelson:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Combinatorial Revolution in Knot Theory
                %strong 58
                11 (2011) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://math.mit.edu/~ormsby/nelson-combinatorial-revolution.pdf"}> pdf
                , full issue:
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/notices/201111/201111FullIssue.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Lauda"}> Aaron Lauda
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Knot theory explained
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/kxaWqKM5JyQ"} YT
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abhijit+Champanerkar"}> Abhijit Champanerkar
                ,
                %em The geometry of knot complements
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.csi.cuny.edu/~abhijit/talks/knot-geometry-h.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/ChampanerkarKnotComplements.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Roland van der Veen:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A smooth introduction to knots
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.julianlyczak.nl/seminar/knots2016-files/KnotesJan18.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/vdVeen-SmoothKnots.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Monographs:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+H.+Crowell"}> Richard H. Crowell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+H.+Fox"} R. H. Fox
                = succeed "," do
